  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "All four completed experiments used singleprofile, so the impact of multiprofile aggregation is the largest unexplored design dimension. Our best results (config_009: 0.4214, config_002: 0.4224) both use scgpt + weighted fusion in multimodal mode, with only a marginal difference between resnet50 and imagenet_vit_l. Config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the most controlled extension of our best singleprofile config: it keeps the same RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy while introducing multiprofile with a simple, robust avgpool aggregation. This isolates the effect of multi-profile aggregation and tells us whether capturing multiple spatial profiles can push accuracy beyond the ~0.42 plateau. With 5 experiments remaining, resolving whether multiprofile is a productive direction is critical before committing further budget to more complex variants (transformer aggregation, different encoders)."
}

